.TH ROX 1 "September 2026" "Rox-Filer2 2.13.0-8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rox, roxfiler, Rox-Filer2, ROX-Filer \- open the Rox-Filer2 file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rox
.RB [ --classic | --modern ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ paths ...]
.br
.B rox-wayland
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ paths ...]
.br
.B rox-x11
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ paths ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rox-Filer2 is a GTK3 continuation of ROX-Filer. It can open filer windows,
manage the ROX desktop and use either X11/XLibre or Wayland at runtime.
.PP
.B rox-wayland
requires an active Wayland display and selects the Wayland backend.
.B rox-x11
requires an active X11/XLibre display and selects the X11 backend.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --classic
Open this invocation with the Classic ROX interface. The saved Interface choice is not changed.
.TP
.B --modern
Open this invocation with the Modern interface. The saved Interface choice is not changed.
.PP
The interface switches also work with
.B rox-x11
and
.B rox-wayland
(for example, \fBrox-x11 --classic\fR or \fBrox-wayland --modern\fR).
.PP
Run
.B rox --help
for the complete list of options supported by the installed version.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/rox.sourceforge.net/ROX-Filer/
contains per-user Rox-Filer2 configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rox-find (1)
